[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387814178","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111463#issuecomment-3387814178","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111463","id":3387814178,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J7fEi","user":{"login":"WesleyClements","id":7082109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODIxMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7082109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements","html_url":"https://github.com/WesleyClements","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T23:55:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T00:01:01Z","body":"This is not a limitation of Godot. You are looking to configure a group of CanvasItems that will receive lights and shadows and another that will only receive light. This is the purpose of CanvasItem's light_mask property.\n\nThe current configuration of your MRP is as such:\n - The light is configured to cast light and shadows on render layer 1 (item_cull_mask)\n - The TileSet's occlusion layer is set block lights on render layer 1 (occusion_layers[0].light_mask)\n - The TileMapLayer and the ColorRect are set to receive lights from render layer 1 (light_mask)\n\nTo get the result that you are desiring, we just need to change the TileMapLayer to receive lights from a different layer. To do this, change the TileMapLayer's light_mask property to only receive lights from render layer 2.\n\n<img width=\"549\" height=\"528\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23ea05b3-5764-4d40-9f2d-2969f638a98d\" />\n\nYou will also need to make sure that the PointLight2D is set to emit light on render layer 2. Importantly we will not set the PointLight2D to cast shadows on render layer 2.\n\n<img width=\"550\" height=\"629\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78f5b47f-c1ee-4d53-b728-4987769200c4\" />\n\nRender layers are worth looking into more!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387814178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3388831321","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111463#issuecomment-3388831321","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111463","id":3388831321,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J_XZZ","user":{"login":"aleks-313","id":148381480,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNgfKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148381480?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313","html_url":"https://github.com/aleks-313","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T08:25:13Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T08:25:13Z","body":"Hi Wesley! Thank you for the quick response and explanation.\n\nI understand how rendering layers help us here, but I believe there are cases in which this approach isn't enough. I've changed the MRP to simulate a \"wall\" that has a right turn. As you can see, the wall tile after the turn is still getting lit up, despite not being in line of sight of the light.\n\n[bug2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22843311/bug2.zip)\n\nI'll also add screenshots of the concrete case I'm working with\n\n<img width=\"613\" height=\"340\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/39f933fb-74b1-448b-bbd5-c8ccbdf9795c\" />\n<img width=\"536\" height=\"355\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9871cb5-f412-4b2a-8e34-df4ac06c5b42\" />\n\nThe approach here isn't exactly what you said (which I've applied in the MRP), but it's quite similar. I have two pointlights, one of which casts shadows on layer 1, and the second of which does not cast shadows on that same layer 1. I've tinted this second light purple to show the difference. \nMy issue is the wall behind the corner being lit up by the second light, when realistically that light shouldn't be reaching it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3388831321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3389118886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111463#issuecomment-3389118886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111463","id":3389118886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KAdmm","user":{"login":"WesleyClements","id":7082109,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODIxMDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7082109?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements","html_url":"https://github.com/WesleyClements","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WesleyClements/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T09:46:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T09:46:32Z","body":"This definitely is a more complicated situation! I believe I've run into this problem as well and spent a lot of time trying to resolve it. There definitely isn't a simple solution but there are remedies. A good starting point is adding a shader to the TileMapLayer that uses a normal map and the direction of the light to choose whether to apply the light texture. Another avenue to explore is using occluders on more than one layer. Here is a revision of the second example that you gave that is closer (but not exactly) to what you want. [example.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22846988/example.zip) The biggest problem with this example is that the light and shadows from all the lights are being applied to all parts of the tiles. We can remedy that by breaking our tiles up into separate parts (like side walls and wall faces), each on their own TileMapLayer, and rendering them into separate SubViewports that are displayed on top of each other. There is a talk by Raffaele Picca on the Godot Engine YouTube channel that discusses what is possible with viewports. He solved a similar problem for Dome Keeper. I'm not speaking for the Godot team, just trying to be helpful. I hope my suggestions might help you find a solution that doesn't require you waiting for a change to the engine!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3389118886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3391926231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111463#issuecomment-3391926231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111463","id":3391926231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KLK_X","user":{"login":"aleks-313","id":148381480,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNgfKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148381480?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313","html_url":"https://github.com/aleks-313","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T19:09:21Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T19:09:21Z","body":"Yeah, that sounds like a solution, at least for now!\n\nThank you very much for your help!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3391926231/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3697926902","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111463#issuecomment-3697926902","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111463","id":3697926902,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7caeL2","user":{"login":"ancrus","id":198895191,"node_id":"U_kgDOC9rmVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198895191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus","html_url":"https://github.com/ancrus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ancrus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T00:39:18Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T00:39:18Z","body":"Why this is closed tho?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3697926902/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":